reviewer_concerns.value:
The initial skepticism from the reviewers was substantially alleviated through additional experiments, clarifications, and rebuttals. Some common concerns are listed as below.
(i) Overly broad or overstated scope claims (e.g., "scientific discovery", "end-to-end workflows");
(ii) Insufficient clarity on evaluation methodology and setup;
(iii) Fairness and completeness of model evaluation (compute, tokens, reasoning modes);
(iv) Evaluation metrics being too coarse (pass or fail only);
(v) Need for stronger transparency and reproducibility details;
(vi) Some presentation and readability issues.

The author has actively participated in conversations with reviewers and received positive responses. The reviewers have reached the consensus of accepting this paper. All major objections were addressed.  I suggest the author to consider the below improvements: (i) Move critical methodological details into the main text with explicit appendix pointers. (ii) Improve table readability and clarity. (iii) Tone down "scientific discovery" claims and sharpen positioning around scientific tool-use and execution.(iv) Explicitly document evaluation setup, costs, human baselines, and difficulty definitions.
